{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956912-why-does-the-small-frame-merit-cost-so-much","id":956912,"title":"Why does the Small Frame merit cost so much?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-24T06:34:44-07:00","id":956912,"title":"Why does the Small Frame merit cost so much?","content":"It just seems really overpriced for lowering your speed, health, and making you more vulnerable to grapples. <br /> It cost 2 exp, and im leaning toward asking the storyteller to make it free, since it has as much of a drawback as a benifit. Is there some sort of benefit to to having small size that makes this merit worthwhile that I'm missing, or am I better off just keeping my strength and stamina 1 dot to reflect my characters small size?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-24-2016, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T06:46:20-07:00","id":956917,"title":"","content":"It works better as a Persistent Condition than a Merit, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T06:49:17-07:00","id":956918,"title":"","content":"Do people use persistent conditions like flaws in other games? I had never heard of doing it like that, don't recall having seen it in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T06:53:37-07:00","id":956921,"title":"","content":"I do. Persistent Conditions are a fantastic design space to put things that don't fit merits in. Stuff like being addicted, a heir to a fortune, mysteriously sick, having a loyal dog, being in love...<br /> If it isn't explored in books, then it's a shame, because it serves us well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:04:22-07:00","id":956926,"title":"","content":"Cool idea. Do you get beats for it whenever it limits you? How much per chapter is allowed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:11:55-07:00","id":956936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956912-why-does-the-small-frame-merit-cost-so-much?p=956926#post956926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool idea. Do you get beats for it whenever it limits you? How much per chapter is allowed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>, but I'd assume you treat it just like any other Condition. If it is a &quot;flaw&quot;, treat it like any other negative Condition and give it a Beat line. Limits are per scene, I think (but remember you can only get 1 Beat from Conditions per Scene).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:12:37-07:00","id":956937,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine Chronicle says, 'Conditions replace the Flaws rules in the World of Darkness Rulebook.'<br /> <br /> Presumably they didn't put it in the second edition book because the GMC was an addendum, while the second edition book is its own system where there's no Flaws rules to replace. It does however explain that Conditions can and should be used for basically anything that affects the characters, and <br /> 'Once per chapter, a player can gain a Beat when a Persistent Condition impacts his character\u2019s life.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-24-2016, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:14:22-07:00","id":956938,"title":"","content":"You do. That's their point :P. We usually go with 1 negative persistent condition and one neutral/positive persistent condition at chargen, though it's mostly because it's a convenient number (it's not a rule). For example, we have a character who is A Teenage Schoolgirl, which is a negative condition due to the fact that it limits her and provides with certain drawbacks, but she also is Bonded with her pretty impressive animal (it's a Mage game); *of course* the animal also can provide beats by being a rebellous komodo dragon who likes to dig graves and eat corpses :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:32:26-07:00","id":956954,"title":"","content":"Well, if you're using the Chase system, being smaller gives a good bonus. Also, from my point of view, smaller characters receive bonuses while being stealthy (more appropriately, their opponents receive penalties for spotting them).<br /> <br /> But yeah, Giant &amp; Small-Framed both seem overcosted, even when you factor all these things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T08:10:28-07:00","id":956972,"title":"","content":"In real life, I have Growth Hormone Deficiency (it was diagnosed when I was four or five). That basically means that a child's body either doesn't produce any growth hormone, that it doesn't produce enough, or that it produces it but doesn't go where it's supposed to. I had constant bloodword during diagnosis, and daily injections of human growth hormone from four or five until my bone age was thirteen or fourteen (I forget which). Would it be helpful if I talked about my real life experiences? Maybe you could find ways to code some of them mechanically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T08:13:47-07:00","id":956975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956912-why-does-the-small-frame-merit-cost-so-much?p=956972#post956972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In real life, I have Growth Hormone Deficiency (it was diagnosed when I was four or five). That basically means that a child's body either doesn't produce any growth hormone, that it doesn't produce enough, or that it produces it but doesn't go where it's supposed to. I had constant bloodword during diagnosis, and daily injections of human growth hormone from four or five until my bone age was thirteen or fourteen (I forget which). Would it be helpful if I talked about my real life experiences? Maybe you could find ways to code some of them mechanically?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds surprisingly interesting. Please do","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T08:33:16-07:00","id":956986,"title":"","content":"As a child, I was extremely tiny, always. Lack of growth hormone meant that without treatment, all of my development would be delayed or not happen at all, including puberty. But as I said, I started treatment at four or five. I don't remember very many details from that time. I remember having like three or four blood tests every few months in the beginning, and my mother having to hold me down. I cried, a lot, and to this day (from that and the nightly injections) I have an extreme phobia of blood and of medical procedures involving needles. I remember the blood tests being longer than like. Blood tests you typically have as adults. It's possible my mind is just stretching them out, but I don't think so, because I specifically remember my mother bringing movies for me to watch. Like movies plural. So I'm pretty sure the blood tests went on longer than is typical. I've also read that when they're initially trying to detect those hormone levels, it's difficult because they secrete at one period during the day, so it's possible they extracted blood over a long period to compare the levels throughout the day.<br /> <br /> Anyway. It got so bad that I would cry and lock myself in rooms to avoid getting my shots, when I was maybe six or seven. My mother said we could stop taking them, and then I found out she used to come into my bedroom at night and give them to me while I was asleep, while also using a numbing spray.<br /> <br /> I first grew breasts at eight years old, and that brought about terrible street harassment from grown men. Keep in mind, at this point, I was still extremely short and I looked eight years old, or younger. At this point, my parents would still sit me in a stroller and sneak me into theme parks or pay a younger child's rate. I'm not mentioning this for people to start saying THEY don't prey sexually on children, so please, no one do that. I'm just telling you about my experiences. Thanks. <br /> <br /> Moving on. I first menstruated at ten years old, and my periods were always extremely terrible. I mean, like, the pain was so bad that I couldn't leave the bed for a week at a time, and if I had to go to school, I would stay at the nurse all day every day. This went on until I went on birth control for the pain, which I didn't do until university.<br /> <br /> The medicine was also extremely expensive, by the way, so I was fortunate that my family was pretty wealthy. I don't remember how old I was, but I remember at a point that our insurance wanted to stop covering the injectibles. My endocrinologist and my father (he's a lawyer) had this long battle with the insurance company, and they kept paying for it, but it's hard to have to travel with medicine that has to be kept cold. Needles on planes, all of this stuff. Most hotels provided fridges for free because it was a medical necessity.<br /> <br /> Now, I'll be twenty-three years old in September. I'm 4'9&quot; and I weigh 82 lbs. People will sometimes still think I'm extremely young if their eyes just glaze over me or I'm with my parents. My baby sister is six years younger than me, and she's taller than I am. People will frequently say shit to me like, &quot;I know you're disabled, but you're like a model anyway&quot;. Don't say that shit to people. That's harmful as hell.<br /> <br /> I still consider myself disabled. There are bit things and small things. Small thing--most cars where the passenger seat only turns on the airbag if a child's not sitting there decide it by weight, and I apparently don't weigh enough for the airbag to turn on, so that's kind of dangerous.<br /> <br /> But yeah. I know I started rambling by the end. Feel free to ask any questions.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it should be a Condition, not a Merit, but I guess that also depends on whether or not you're talking about an actual disability like what I have, or just an adult who's kind of short.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:01:47-07:00","id":957048,"title":"","content":"Thank you, for that. <hr />Thinking about the effects of such a Condition mechanically, other than the obvious systems ramifications due to Size, what else is there? I'd be leery of attributing any kind of Social effect (the common tendency of society to disregard anyone even vaguely child-like be damned), since that is highly contextual. Issues with Item Availability? Body Armor can't be easy to come by at that size. Effects on things like Knockdown maneuvers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:19:19-07:00","id":957061,"title":"","content":"In such open ended condition, I would just go with reduced Size (and not always) and &quot;-1, -2 or +1 to appropiate rolls&quot; with a list of examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:30:51-07:00","id":957070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness